# Frontend

- **Design source of truth:** [docs/prd/design.md](../../docs/prd/design.md) — tokens (Baloo 2 / Nunito), Lucide-first icons, Fernsehnachmittag layout §9, desktop-first + stacked mobile.
- Text is the default medium (squad lists, reports, inbox, dialogue), but
  it is not mandatory. Morale, financial health, match momentum,
  staff/player quality, and relationships should be represented visually
  (color, icons, small charts, SVG/CSS) rather than as raw
  numbers in a table, wherever that communicates better.
- Pitch and stadium-editor visuals: SVG components, 2D only. No 3D
  libraries, no WebGL unless explicitly requested.
- Aim for a game cockpit — hero panels (pitch, charts, heatmaps) before naked tables where design §9 shows it; FM2001 density still allowed for league/transfer tables.
- Match commentary feed and pitch visualization are two views of the same
  match-event stream; keep their data source shared (e.g. one hook/context
  feeding both), not two independently polled/fetched states.
- **Platforms (PRD 09 / 14 / 17):** Ship for desktop browser and Steam Deck
  first. Still design and test layouts **mobile-responsive** (narrow viewport,
  touch targets) so PWA/phone testing works; mobile is bonus, not a separate
  product fork.
